#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ccd2293-eb0e-5503-8406-7eaa88cc133f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/0c/0cc1d91f18ad1c335e4a9a95a7c97a0bb899597af82abb1ffdf7c0650200e9eb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699577} {:answer/id #uuid "223c5e59-3a53-518e-99d2-280a2f535ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/2c/2c1666e7a50748cd375ce556176ceb7a2edeb8c5d837cbfb593a6dae6cccab54.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699579} {:answer/id #uuid "63de9413-df4d-5a79-ba67-9ca222d41e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ab/ab38dc8884f5e665d31b40193057d5af1665d1b0d582aca85cad2ee5fee8ed3c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699584} {:answer/id #uuid "6dee476e-780e-50ab-b392-8f62f9c3df96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/f4/f4cc453b7166e4b7cde1a3ad12c8aa6b25c7419e1447a533b4cf40105aa359e4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699585} {:answer/id #uuid "8a4f82b3-02f8-5c61-94fa-c05d38cda737" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/1f/1f30a5bd1c3094e9f37b157de9ddc1aea376bf94f426fb7010b343213f80ab2c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699589}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699584} :answer-field/id #uuid "73378799-4cc1-54e0-af58-da11ea9dc550" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699586}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "02bb3cbb-abee-5c30-8079-ac2b1489215f" :question/problem "Which diagram represents\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=-x\\,\\mathbf i-y\\,\\mathbf j\n$$\n\nat $A=(-2,1)$, $B=(1,2)$, and $C=(2,-2)$?\n\nEvaluate the two components at each point, then place the tail of its vector at that point. All diagrams use the same scale, with one unit per grid interval." :question/worked-solution "Substitute each point into $\\mathbf F(x,y)=-x\\,\\mathbf i-y\\,\\mathbf j$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(-2,1)&=-(-2)\\,\\mathbf i-(1)\\,\\mathbf j=2\\,\\mathbf i-\\mathbf j \\\\\n\\mathbf F(1,2)&=-(1)\\,\\mathbf i-(2)\\,\\mathbf j=-\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j \\\\\n\\mathbf F(2,-2)&=-(2)\\,\\mathbf i-(-2)\\,\\mathbf j=-2\\,\\mathbf i+2\\,\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlace each tail at its point: from $A$ go 2 units right and 1 down; from $B$ go 1 left and 2 down; from $C$ go 2 left and 2 up. The vectors point toward the origin. The correct diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/ab/ab38dc8884f5e665d31b40193057d5af1665d1b0d582aca85cad2ee5fee8ed3c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699580 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bb90f32-89f2-5d99-9737-5e9e1ca8c70c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/05/05f03f531dbac4d3cfec041e444c47ce2d2ec6b5a01b8d316fe089d37ba9afcc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699576} {:answer/id #uuid "8912ac65-e717-5381-9bf6-2d58552daf10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/bb/bbb0d965c7ec72ee8008b34972172af8cc5635df3d963dd27183a8f21b7f416d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699588} {:answer/id #uuid "8b30d0ac-2872-508b-b8fe-3739c8550d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/45/45d92334e0129a9b3d3262664074b630066573703fef55c6bc804ec717066e69.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699590} {:answer/id #uuid "9b3461fd-6a84-5a93-bcaf-0ee5845013f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/eb/eb9cc13997a1fb7b1c56018ceb3df13d1d87033f16b607b85fa48e113a52c802.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699594} {:answer/id #uuid "e2d82c8a-464c-5b59-ba7d-24915ff57000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/40/4059b6c9b926eea8ec523769d4858715f28ae316627f111fe08ca721df17ed28.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699601}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699588} :answer-field/id #uuid "b218c9c3-cd15-5233-ba41-b80fc27fdad2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699597}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "36301cba-bb7d-56d6-bf60-1510c1ba0e9f" :question/problem "Which diagram represents\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=(y-x)\\,\\mathbf i+(x+y)\\,\\mathbf j\n$$\n\nat $A=(-2,1)$, $B=(1,1)$, and $C=(2,-2)$? All diagrams use one unit per grid interval." :question/worked-solution "Evaluate both components at each point, keeping their order: the $\\mathbf i$ component is horizontal and the $\\mathbf j$ component is vertical.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(-2,1)&=(1-(-2))\\,\\mathbf i+(-2+1)\\,\\mathbf j=3\\,\\mathbf i-\\mathbf j \\\\\n\\mathbf F(1,1)&=(1-1)\\,\\mathbf i+(1+1)\\,\\mathbf j=2\\,\\mathbf j \\\\\n\\mathbf F(2,-2)&=(-2-2)\\,\\mathbf i+(2+(-2))\\,\\mathbf j=-4\\,\\mathbf i.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the arrow at $A$ goes 3 right and 1 down, the arrow at $B$ goes straight up 2 units, and the arrow at $C$ goes straight left 4 units. A zero component removes motion along that axis; it does not remove the other component. Keep each tail at its labeled point and check all three arrows.\n\n![](images/bb/bbb0d965c7ec72ee8008b34972172af8cc5635df3d963dd27183a8f21b7f416d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699603 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04b6dd27-4b23-5629-928b-935d284ece38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/00/0021413d66ea6423e35f3e2d67083509ce9d5442feed04964586ebe0739727fa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699574} {:answer/id #uuid "1fda1b22-e592-523f-9dfd-32f9952c40d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/4b/4bf7b2086637023ea65047fc42646a0bd2f9c4a6ca7f0135470c753038fe721b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699578} {:answer/id #uuid "9cc2f2f7-30dc-55fe-9c20-10e0f5a388ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/90/908a6bdba9f909405af82e26c47e1a61eb8f60968b46a87127dfe8d5e86c34e7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699595} {:answer/id #uu