:answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699605}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699605} :answer-field/id #uuid "9050ced3-4b2e-5238-93ad-c870bf2249f8" :answer-field/key "C y-coordinate" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699592} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e5c8a85-65e0-53f7-b1ef-be3e453f084b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699587}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699587} :answer-field/id #uuid "93209eeb-585f-55e6-9089-cb5f9557c4e8" :answer-field/key "B y-coordinate" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699593} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d313c666-4a58-5241-a02c-3619ad7020d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699599}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699599} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3ce8e7f-0893-55e4-9093-c35f6e863783" :answer-field/key "B x-coordinate" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699602}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e9f9252b-5e19-5c34-b143-ee99843a434b" :question/problem "Sketch the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=-xy\\,\\mathbf i+x^2\\,\\mathbf j\n$$\n\nat $A=(-2,1)$, $B=(1,-1)$, and $C=(2,-1)$ by completing both tasks. All diagrams use one unit per grid interval.\n\nEnter the coordinates of the arrowhead for each vector when its tail is at the stated point.\n\nArrowhead from $A$: $(${{A x-coordinate}}$,\\,${{A y-coordinate}}$)$\n\nArrowhead from $B$: $(${{B x-coordinate}}$,\\,${{B y-coordinate}}$)$\n\nArrowhead from $C$: $(${{C x-coordinate}}$,\\,${{C y-coordinate}}$)$\n\nChoose the correct diagram below." :question/worked-solution "First evaluate the field, treating $-xy$ as the negative of the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(-2,1)&=-(-2)(1)\\,\\mathbf i+(-2)^2\\,\\mathbf j=2\\,\\mathbf i+4\\,\\mathbf j \\\\\n\\mathbf F(1,-1)&=-(1)(-1)\\,\\mathbf i+1^2\\,\\mathbf j=\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j \\\\\n\\mathbf F(2,-1)&=-(2)(-1)\\,\\mathbf i+2^2\\,\\mathbf j=2\\,\\mathbf i+4\\,\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors all point up and right, so direction alone cannot select a diagram. Their horizontal and vertical displacements must also match: $(2,4)$ at $A$, $(1,1)$ at $B$, and $(2,4)$ at $C$.\n\nThe field value gives a displacement, not the arrowhead's coordinates. Add each displacement to its tail:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA+\\mathbf F(A)&=(-2+2,\\,1+4)=(0,5),\\\\\nB+\\mathbf F(B)&=(1+1,\\,-1+1)=(2,0),\\\\\nC+\\mathbf F(C)&=(2+2,\\,-1+4)=(4,3).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors at $A$ and $C$ have equal components but different tails and arrowheads. The resulting diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/00/009e26f3566e0a28d8b74b970ed4e18fab0e42079051764e50124cbc43fba278.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a8f93fe-9624-58ca-b181-c8db155547a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/4c/4c86c3ffe220532d2e61d7d3eb43328131849ba0551aa197ab5c45e503c3ed5f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699896} {:answer/id #uuid "87d697b9-53b5-570e-a3bd-8089cdbc0605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/3d/3dc1cb0a1fc04e960aa082f3519d346f2eb1229106ed76353cb95fbe4f91deb0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699912} {:answer/id #uuid "87de592f-6c0a-5694-aaf9-e6f565b33055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/cb/cb244b77cb36032c0034678bbb3fd2f10d24375b9c87575be92645e34d4dd88a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699913} {:answer/id #uuid "af714f7d-d6f6-5da4-a707-9e28e77ba131" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/86/863b21b4ee72557a665bf8d31dac02162934c6bfd1b4e7cccc88787d1dde9d16.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699917} {:answer/id #uuid "e2797b9f-a58c-5f29-8673-6c2b5ebf51c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/f9/f9a5c6caec97630e8a14f468b8e51f2cd50cc9880594b5905dd1b92c1b021631.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699927}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699912} :answer-field/id #uuid "71a31d91-bf2d-5121-b1a1-8ff517c99ab0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699909}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "281b2ad3-b25c-5ad0-98e9-0a63349e9d3e" :question/problem "Which diagram represents\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right)\\,i+\\left(|x|\\right)\\,j\n$$\n\nat $A=(0,-1)$, $B=(0,1)$, $C=(1,-3)$? All diagrams use one unit per grid interval.\n\nEvaluate both components at each point, then place the tail of its vector at that point." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$. Substitute into each component, then combine the results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(0,-1)&=-(-1)\\frac{0}{-1}=0 \\\\\nQ(0,-1)&=-(-1)|0|=0 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(0,-1)&=0 \\\\\nP(0,1)&=-(-1)\\frac{0}{1}=0 \\\\\nQ(0,1)&=-(-1)|0|=0 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(0,1)&=0 \\\\\nP(1,-3)&=-(-1)\\frac{1}{-3}=- \\frac{1}{3} \\\\\nQ(1,-3)&=-(-1)|1|=1 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(1,-3)&=-\\frac{1}{3}\\,i+j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first component gives the horizontal displacement and the second gives the vertical displacement. Place each tail at its labeled point. A zero component gives no displacement along that axis; a zero vector stays at its tail.\n\n![](images/3d/3dc1cb0a1fc04e960aa082f3519d346f2eb1229106ed76353cb95fbe4f91deb0.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699901 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bb29d72-87e6-57ed-932e-7cfd0a03f1e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/59/59bf4b515e94e726d3af8a991cfdfd54927e994e664d87a757534bb430ed92c5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699903} {:answer/id #uuid "5803fb47-99ed-5613-ae31-83bdc384b7f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/aa/aa18b272c87bb5222ba7e66adc7524fc1c517892ba4342fef7a02d565f26c31c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699904} {:answer/id #uuid "6eaeaa7e-f25c-5a2e-918a-3856926dadfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/6d/6d9c8a73be1513468cd478684f4e81bd6a058ca847c023245004bdca47704bfd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699908} {:answer/id #uuid "7a8ad149-0e6b-5585-80de-c47a784c2ee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/c1/c1b4d360b19d0239c82bf7c4f03ddcfeb572c896ca9b86e06f2d58576bf6d58f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699910} {:answer/id #uuid "b26fec01-78af-5715-8788-59e6f1ff7c62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/be/be050faf24136c77177b5cdeb82fe5a5e0e6dd3245a0604474ea00611c91608d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699919}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699903} :answer-field/id #uuid "335ea5a3-58c1-524e-8035-7ad37f471639" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699900}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "37ecfed8-4569-5c5e-94c9-a4ff1f97904d" :question/problem "Which diagram represents\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(\\frac{y}{xy+1}\\right)\\,i+\\left(\\frac{x}{xy+1}\\right)\\,j\n$$\n\nat $A=(0,3)$, $B=(1,0)$, $C=(3,-1)$? All diagrams use one unit per grid interval.\n\nEvaluate both components at each point, then place the tail of its vector at that point." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$. Substitute into each component, then combine the results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(0,3)&=\\frac{(1)(3)}{(0)(3)+1}=3 \\\\\nQ(0,3)&=\\frac{(1)(0)}{(0)(3)+1}=0 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(0,3)&=3\\,i \\\\\nP(1,0)&=\\frac{(1)(0)}{(1)(0)+1}=0 \\\\\nQ(1,0)&=\\frac{(1)(1)}{(1)(0)+1}=1 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(1,0)&=j \\\\\nP(3,-1)&=\\frac{(1)(-1)}{(3)(-1)+1}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\\nQ(3,-1)&=\\frac{(1)(3)}{(3)(-1)+1}=- \\frac{3}{2} \\\\\n\\mathbf F(3,-1)&=\\frac{1}{2}\\,i-\\frac{3}{2}\\,j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first component gives the horizontal displacement and the second gives the vertical displacement. Place each tail at its labeled point. A zero component gives no displacement along that axis; a zero vector stays at its tail.\n\n![](images/59/59bf4b515e94e726d3af8a991cfdfd54927e994e664d87a757534bb430ed92c5.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699906 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "177a26ed-62f6-5f1a-b955-0f9e1632ef32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/dc/dca5659208c862497f2052ddbd5d7672d6336d154c818900cc4fccec425dfec9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699895} {:answer/id #uuid "3a74ddf3-f157-567d-95dc-3894c6539e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/e1/e1d69cfb0de2d24a16d10426d5632cb7d84bddb31628ae84336619cb0cdff9da.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699902} {:answer/id #uuid "b0db5701-fa3c-50e6-b5ec-eb607382a469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/75/753510ef5f4fed587eb11988029c50b9fb92912045e1bf7b99fd094d1fb14f7a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699918} {:answer/id #uuid "c73b864b-a6e1-5cee-b87d-d73194523892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/76/76391d7e3fc8332a1dbae465a607eee0ce143f2dd8d272162cf45ab3e374fe19.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699923} {:answer/id #uuid "d82eb334-ce62-5132-a664-dd569aaad933" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/8d/8df0c8ea5dc6fe03bf070c2ca8a899715f9b627f11bbb756e8a27cdabdbae663.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699925}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699925} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab3c1670-fbe3-5eb9-bb21-623782d48ebd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699916}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6231ff82-79b5-51d4-ac0f-c977c7f4683e" :question/problem "Which diagram represents\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(y-2x\\right)\\,i+\\left(-2y+4x\\right)\\,j\n$$\n\nat $A=(1,0)$, $B=(0,0)$, $C=(0,-2)$? All diagrams use one unit per grid interval.\n\nEvaluate both components at each point, then place the tail of its vector at that point." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$. Substitute into each component, then combine the results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(1,0)&=(0)-(2)(1)=-2 \\\\\nQ(1,0)&=(-2)(0)-(2)(-2)(1)=4 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(1,0)&=-2\\,i+4\\,j \\\\\nP(0,0)&=(0)-(2)(0)=0 \\\\\nQ(0,0)&=(-2)(0)-(2)(-2)(0)=0 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(0,0)&=0 \\\\\nP(0,-2)&=(-2)-(2)(0)=-2 \\\\\nQ(0,-2)&=(-2)(-2)-(2)(-2)(0)=4 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(0,-2)&=-2\\,i+4\\,j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first component gives the horizontal displacement and the second gives the vertical displacement. Place each tail at its labeled point. A zero component gives no displacement along that axis; a zero vector stays at its tail.\n\n![](images/8d/8df0c8ea5dc6fe03bf070c2ca8a899715f9b627f11bbb756e8a27cdabdbae663.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699911 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d1f5735-d5e8-54aa-99bb-1674000106b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/fb/fb6f667089062d7c406a208dd2377f9941ce1d39e4206f78f7425f93c7252153.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699897} {:answer/id #uuid "6a9cdd7e-1468-55ab-b80d-d67caf0c41cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/80/80baba867a547b0c71a308ecf0a051d10ec74e494731d00aac1bd42ea25e8a98.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699907} {:answer/id #uuid "b28fb461-6de0-5538-9f14-3cc26f2591fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/fa/fa48d5e504372b6cdfbf86cf8a4bd510073cd068ed47a5159ae354c20224c8a0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699920} {:answer/id #uuid "c14d9f4f-2379-502e-9587-7a92270dfae1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ea/ea7815bafb1b211486b44c0cc7de9f64ad69576e925809102e005de3c34d670e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699921} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf6e92c-b5d3-510c-a410-930f6a74bdd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/aa/aa5216de6120e354d0e64a6d03209f70cf611b4417b4e795b11f94e3853b939f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699926}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699907} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe9fa03a-d43e-5011-b20a-0581b6697399" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7be3def5-ca38-5d81-817b-90672d97ad53" :question/problem "Which diagram represents\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(3\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi x}{2}\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left(-xy\\right)\\,j\n$$\n\nat $A=(0,2)$, $B=(-3,-2)$, $C=(2,-1)$? All diagrams use one unit per grid interval.\n\nEvaluate both components at each point, then place the tail of its vector at that point." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$. Substitute into each component, then combine the results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(0,2)&=(3)\\sin(0)=0 \\\\\nQ(0,2)&=(-1)(0)(2)=0 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(0,2)&=0 \\\\\nP(-3,-2)&=(3)\\sin\\left(- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\right)=3 \\\\\nQ(-3,-2)&=(-1)(-3)(-2)=-6 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(-3,-2)&=3\\,i-6\\,j \\\\\nP(2,-1)&=(3)\\sin(\\pi)=0 \\\\\nQ(2,-1)&=(-1)(2)(-1)=2 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(2,-1)&=2\\,j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first component gives the horizontal displacement and the second gives the vertical displacement. Place each tail at its labeled point. A zero component gives no displacement along that axis; a zero vector stays at its tail.\n\n![](images/80/80baba867a547b0c71a308ecf0a051d10ec74e494731d00aac1bd42ea25e8a98.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699914 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ecc6fda-39d2-5890-8c70-ae23d62217fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/47/47d19b0ab827362425b410fbb97374b1ff1e5fb615598893489b2c5cc7f61a65.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699898} {:answer/id #uuid "a1e24318-9c3c-5624-98b3-fb8f796aae5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/6a/6ad801d03665b00b88d4ca68d8db3bcd750f534f6cdc91961f452478a241780e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699915} {:answer/id #uuid "c1b18bc2-1c78-548f-b8ea-37598585fef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/eb/ebfa711c34087c27db58698321ac3fc18bd109752c885afafbf1de8d8131689e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699922} {:answer/id #uuid "d5f0b116-690e-5a42-a252-535567139fce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/c0/c0c044853126c7a31383af8110c438d0e185c53ebecdc4086f58322cde8d8d4b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699924} {:answer/id #uuid "f7c3a8dd-0057-5c52-a26e-01328cbbdd91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/21/21b0f5411583f6081934b98d9c01c78c3a17292c2b7b9282e66ed7fe3c2fb3c8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699928}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699898} :answer-field/id #uuid "58376643-1a7f-5911-8161-c8d6282d7650" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a071c0b2-b12a-59cd-bc7b-1824a457b80f" :question/problem "Which diagram represents\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(\\frac{2y}{1-y}\\right)\\,i+\\left(\\frac{x}{y-1}\\right)\\,j\n$$\n\nat $A=(1,-2)$, $B=(-3,0)$, $C=(0,3)$? All diagrams use one unit per grid interval.\n\nEvaluate both components at each point, then place the tail of its vector at that point." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$. Substitute into each component, then combine the results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(1,-2)&=\\frac{(2)(-2)}{1-(-2)}=- \\frac{4}{3} \\\\\nQ(1,-2)&=\\frac{(1)(1)}{(-2)-1}=- \\frac{1}{3} \\\\\n\\mathbf F(1,-2)&=-\\frac{4}{3}\\,i-\\frac{1}{3}\\,j \\\\\nP(-3,0)&=\\frac{(2)(0)}{1-(0)}=0 \\\\\nQ(-3,0)&=\\frac{(1)(-3)}{(0)-1}=3 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(-3,0)&=3\\,j \\\\\nP(0,3)&=\\frac{(2)(3)}{1-(3)}=-3 \\\\\nQ(0,3)&=\\frac{(1)(0)}{(3)-1}=0 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(0,3)&=-3\\,i\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first component gives the horizontal displacement and the second gives the vertical displacement. Place each tail at its labeled point. A zero component gives no displacement along that axis; a zero vector stays at its tail.\n\n![](images/47/47d19b0ab827362425b410fbb97374b1ff1e5fb615598893489b2c5cc7f61a65.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702015 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe52663f-3831-508c-80aa-5011cf978661" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702025}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702025} :answer-field/id #uuid "db828325-2956-512c-b92f-44ecc57a6df0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702023}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1fd0630f-5b94-5ac5-b47d-675936a7a80e" :question/problem "If\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthen $\\det(B)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Expand across the top row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Each minor is the $2\\times2$ determinant left after deleting the entry's row and column. Write $M_{1j}$ for the minor of the entry in column $j$ of the top row.\n\nThe third top-row entry is zero, so its term vanishes. The other two minors are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M_{11}&=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}=1\\cdot3-2\\cdot(-2)=7, \\\\ M_{12}&=\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}=(-3)\\cdot3-2\\cdot1=-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the top-row expansion:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(B)&=2M_{11}-(-1)M_{12}+0M_{13} \\\\ &=2(7)-(-1)(-11) \\\\ &=14-11 \\\\ &=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtracting the negative middle entry gives a positive multiplier, but its minor is $-11$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702017 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e07a8a4-573c-5ee7-b50a-aca64454ab73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702016}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702016} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9e2a880-49cc-581c-b603-45bca68c7151" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702024}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "46aaf14e-bed6-5539-b24d-ab655167ab9f" :question/problem "If\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthen $\\det(C)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Expand across the top row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Each minor is the $2\\times2$ determinant left after deleting the entry's row and column. Write $M_{1j}$ for the minor of the entry in column $j$ of the top row.\n\nAll three terms must be evaluated. First calculate the minors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M_{11}&=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}=2\\cdot1-(-2)(-3)=-4, \\\\ M_{12}&=\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}=(-1)\\cdot1-(-2)\\cdot3=5, \\\\ M_{13}&=\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{vmatrix}=(-1)(-3)-2\\cdot3=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen combine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(C)&=2M_{11}-(-1)M_{12}+3M_{13} \\\\ &=2(-4)-(-1)(5)+3(-3) \\\\ &=-8+5-9 \\\\ &=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the sign of each entry separate from the alternating expansion signs. In particular, the middle contribution is $+5$, while the last contribution is $-9$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b588765-a38b-52a9-8290-4c6e3625ee4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702014} {:answer/id #uuid "6daa9a67-611e-5d79-95bc-9d2612ecf94d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702018} {:answer/id #uuid "7099badf-ec8a-53ea-bdb4-f3a4ead31df9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702019} {:answer/id #uuid "72f3aa9c-27f0-5cbd-8408-af58cc0177b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702020} {:answer/id #uuid "876b652b-752d-5329-94b0-5be7322dd82e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702021}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702018} :answer-field/id #uuid "19e8b6e0-5747-53ac-bedf-2ceb874492fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702013}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9bbb6c9f-0926-5f9e-832d-70a515e13083" :question/problem "Find $\\det(A)$ for\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Expand across the top row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Each minor is the $2\\times2$ determinant left after deleting the entry's row and column.\n\nThe first and third terms vanish because their top-row entries are zero. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(A)&=-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=2\\bigl(1\\cdot5-4\\cdot2\\bigr) \\\\ &=2(5-8) \\\\ &=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe negative middle entry and the minus sign in the expansion give a positive multiplier; the minor itself is negative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702041 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c3b81ee-57fc-5dcc-8794-2e8471868dd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702043} {:answer/id #uuid "ee5ecf1e-ed92-5ce9-9697-e38ffd3907c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702069}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702069} :answer-field/id #uuid "0855946d-6186-549c-8c14-c23bdc26f582" :answer-field/key "$B$ is a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702039} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21c576ec-49e6-547d-9d4d-4ea659426772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702046} {:answer/id #uuid "c5749f45-4dee-57d0-b180-4115f0819f1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702066}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702066} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d4fbcd8-6322-5f97-ba46-7c7565ff3612" :answer-field/key "$\\det(B)=\\sqrt{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702054} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e7b35f4-6b6d-5f69-a6cc-4c3334fbb7d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702051} {:answer/id #uuid "5989ebab-0dec-5827-801a-f603fd045f8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702052}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702052} :answer-field/id #uuid "99f8e573-5115-57f9-8f97-c73183c6bf3b" :answer-field/key "$B$ is **not** a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702060}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1b0418f3-cf49-5336-8d8a-0ade16540fca" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $B$?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{2} & -1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 3 & -\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A square matrix is singular if and only if its determinant is zero.\n\nExpand along the top row. In the first minor, $(\\sqrt{2})(-\\sqrt{2})=-2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\det(B) &= 1\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & -1 \\\\ 3 & -\\sqrt{2}\\end{vmatrix}\n-2\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{2}\\end{vmatrix}\n+0\\begin{vmatrix}2 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 1(-2+3)-2(-2\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2})+0 \\\\\n&= 1-2(-\\sqrt{2}) \\\\\n&= 1+2\\sqrt{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\sqrt{2}>0$, the determinant $1+2\\sqrt{2}$ is positive, so it is not zero. Thus $B$ is not singular. Also, $1+2\\sqrt{2}\\ne\\sqrt{2}$, since their difference is $1+\\sqrt{2}>0$.\n\nSelect only “$B$ is not a singular matrix.”"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702063 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76e89e36-2713-5e70-b5b7-661b0c7d213c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702055} {:answer/id #uuid "fe34a2f7-685a-5f24-be6b-0c81532fb58b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702071}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702055} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b0b4a50-d422-5de1-b4cc-06439cecdce3" :answer-field/key "$\\det(Q)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702042} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4bac635-dfe5-56ad-9065-270e52378451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702062} {:answer/id #uuid "c35b47b8-7b51-5e72-b5f8-7b921c167d84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702065}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702062} :answer-field/id #uuid "217b9884-09ba-5d2f-815a-1e8f8abd0ca9" :answer-field/key "$P$ is a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702044} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8da512b5-8fa6-5062-8aa8-e177d8ec7727" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702059} {:answer/id #uuid "b0e49aa8-0627-566d-91be-2b6710da965a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702064}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702064} :answer-field/id #uuid "35796e5b-44d5-5a8f-8177-8d42113c9d80" :answer-field/key "$Q$ has a multiplicative inverse, but $P$ does not" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702048} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f704c5a-cb26-558e-9d35-57016fbba34f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702047} {:answer/id #uuid "7cd6dad2-df3a-5f53-b59d-db62a39c0b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702056}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702056} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f205ecd-c1d5-5c7f-b0f8-540de92c805b" :answer-field/key "$Q$ is a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a752eff2-2eb5-599d-9b15-76e43b68722e" :question/problem "The matrices $P$ and $Q$ differ in just one entry. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nQ=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A square matrix is singular if and only if its determinant is zero. A singular matrix has no multiplicative inverse; a nonsingular square matrix has one.\n\nThe matching first two rows do not determine the determinant by themselves. Expand each determinant along the top row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\det(P) &= 1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\n-2\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\n+1\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= (4-9)-2(8-9)+(6-3) \\\\\n&= -5+2+3 \\\\\n&= 0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe changed entry appears in the first two minors for $Q$, so those minors must be evaluated again:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\det(Q) &= 1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{vmatrix}\n-2\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{vmatrix}\n+1\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= (5-9)-2(10-9)+(6-3) \\\\\n&= -4-2+3 \\\\\n&= -3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $P$ is singular and has no multiplicative inverse. Since $\\det(Q)=-3\\ne0$, $Q$ is not singular and has a multiplicative inverse. A negative determinant is still nonzero, and $\\det(Q)$ is $-3$, not $3$.\n\nSelect “$P$ is a singular matrix” and “$Q$ has a multiplicative inverse, but $P$ does not.”"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702067 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8690d79a-8481-5797-91cf-e57c617b35bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702058} {:answer/id #uuid "dd44f94a-29e8-536f-9d01-a76eaceb6b10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702068}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702068} :answer-field/id #uuid "21b6ad7a-96c0-5a0b-9012-3682455c41f4" :answer-field/key "$A$ is **not** a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702045} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f0576c8-6839-5e8c-a48e-41dea6d03f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702040} {:answer/id #uuid "84b997ce-355d-5c81-92fd-4e1eebeaa835" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702057}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702040} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b644231-7625-5ce4-b5dd-f9d8eeec83c8" :answer-field/key "$\\det(A)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702049} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d78fa22-a938-58ec-9f30-7575b0045b95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702053} {:answer/id #uuid "f6785310-9d47-5e83-acc3-692cb6f61f5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702070}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702053} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2c21450-921b-581c-8f81-6e56d4ed6b27" :answer-field/key "$A$ is a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702061}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dba188e3-8df7-57bd-9cbf-0692250a9150" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $A$?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A square matrix is singular if and only if its determinant is zero.\n\nExpand along the top row, using the signs $+,-,+$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\det(A) &= 0\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\n-1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\n+2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 0-1(4-6)+2(3-4) \\\\\n&= 2-2 \\\\\n&= 0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ is singular. Select $\\det(A)=0$ and “$A$ is a singular matrix.” Do not select “$A$ is not a singular matrix.”"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702134 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11d70b0a-8252-57a2-8ca4-8ef0eae9cefc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(x+y)^2}\\langle x^2y+2xy^2-y^2,\\,x^3+2xy+y^2\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702130} {:answer/id #uuid "7839855c-9d8a-5d19-aa22-81ad076d661d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x+y}\\langle 2xy,\\,x^2+2y\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702137} {:answer/id #uuid "820a3ba9-de53-5b7e-b5f9-08bcca03a641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x+y}\\langle x^2y+2xy^2-y^2,\\,x^3+2xy+y^2\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702138} {:answer/id #uuid "928ec446-4d46-5208-8f62-7d276c7925fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(x+y)^2}\\langle x^2y+2xy^2+y^2,\\,x^3+2x^2y+2xy+3y^2\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702140} {:answer/id #uuid "ca47134c-99d5-52fc-a222-7268296c49c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(x+y)^2}\\langle x^3+2xy+y^2,\\,x^2y+2xy^2-y^2\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702146}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702130} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e629ed0-2f99-542b-a975-4fc9cf29d1d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "32941568-5ac4-5aa1-baf0-9252bbdeb98f" :question/problem "Given $h(x,y)=\\dfrac{x^2y+y^2}{x+y}$, find $\\nabla h(x,y)$ for $x+y\\ne 0$." :question/worked-solution "Let $N=x^2y+y^2$ and $D=x+y$. Treating the other variable as constant gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N_x&=2xy, &D_x&=1, \\\\ N_y&=x^2+2y, &D_y&=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the quotient rule separately to each partial derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h_x(x,y)&=\\frac{(2xy)(x+y)-(x^2y+y^2)}{(x+y)^2} \\\\ &=\\frac{x^2y+2xy^2-y^2}{(x+y)^2}, \\\\ h_y(x,y)&=\\frac{(x^2+2y)(x+y)-(x^2y+y^2)}{(x+y)^2} \\\\ &=\\frac{x^3+2xy+y^2}{(x+y)^2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe denominator-derivative term must be subtracted in both components. Assemble the gradient with $h_x$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla h(x,y)&=\\frac{x^2y+2xy^2-y^2}{(x+y)^2}\\,\\mathbf i \\\\ &\\quad+\\frac{x^3+2xy+y^2}{(x+y)^2}\\,\\mathbf j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis expression is valid on the given domain $x+y\\ne 0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702136 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24be7895-000e-56e9-92c1-86a40897adf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle 4,\\,11\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702132} {:answer/id #uuid "306364ca-2ef6-50c7-86fa-25025601af8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle 2,\\,11\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702133} {:answer/id #uuid "8c6c98bf-c141-5039-89a2-9eb86f052bad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle 10,\\,2\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702139} {:answer/id #uuid "ab085430-144f-5c68-b59a-9aaeaba3eb77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle 2,\\,10\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702145} {:answer/id #uuid "df6a7b7d-9097-573e-aedb-740eb20a1908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle -2,\\,10\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702148}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702145} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca510efd-dcc2-5b90-b749-dae4ad6f7837" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702147}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5f456373-63c1-5584-9cd1-41b8807fa22a" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\nabla f(x,y)$ at $(1,2)$ if $f(x,y)=2x^2-xy+3y^2-y.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiate with respect to one variable at a time, treating the other as constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_x(x,y)&=4x-y+0+0=4x-y \\\\ f_y(x,y)&=0-x+6y-1=-x+6y-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe gradient lists the $x$ partial first and the $y$ partial second:\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y)=\\langle 4x-y,\\,-x+6y-1\\rangle.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the point after differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla f(1,2)&=\\langle 4(1)-2,\\,-1+6(2)-1\\rangle \\\\ &=\\langle 2,\\,10\\rangle.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702141 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24588712-6e75-5337-a7f9-c47f0b63ca63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle \\ln 2+\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702131} {:answer/id #uuid "3f68e687-8845-5fe3-8089-712be93a5b64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle \\ln 2+1,\\,1\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702135} {:answer/id #uuid "a0959a13-0727-57e7-8b32-43c76ef35150" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle \\ln 2+\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\ln 2+\\frac{1}{2}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702143} {:answer/id #uuid "e20ebcce-8f04-5931-bd64-fcf1dcf875d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\ln 2+\\frac{1}{2}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702149} {:answer/id #uuid "fb6a6758-f302-5fdb-a358-1b71fb0a7051" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702150}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702131} :answer-field/id #uuid "a14d5d1c-271d-5909-9bda-0438905d4b3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702144}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "968be986-703b-5484-8f5a-02e456810fcb" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\nabla g(x,y)$ at $(1,1)$ if $g(x,y)=x\\ln(x+y).$" :question/worked-solution "For the $x$ partial, both factors depend on $x$, so use the product rule and the chain rule. For the $y$ partial, $x$ is constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g_x(x,y)&=1\\cdot\\ln(x+y)+x\\cdot\\frac{1}{x+y}\\cdot 1 \\\\ &=\\ln(x+y)+\\frac{x}{x+y}, \\\\ g_y(x,y)&=x\\cdot\\frac{1}{x+y}\\cdot 1=\\frac{x}{x+y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssemble the two partial derivatives in order:\n\n$$\n\\nabla g(x,y)=\\left\\langle\\ln(x+y)+\\frac{x}{x+y},\\,\\frac{x}{x+y}\\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nAt $(1,1)$ the logarithm is defined, since $x+y=2>0$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla g(1,1)&=\\left\\langle\\ln 2+\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\right\\rangle.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702179 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77d070f4-5a75-5f5f-870a-c2f5b8da5eb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702188} {:answer/id #uuid "95d131de-3bbb-560b-95f3-6546bb67144a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702195} {:answer/id #uuid "9b093422-f0fe-5b42-bc86-73490a29577d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702196} {:answer/id #uuid "c2b22e93-507b-5086-897c-531b35d767b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702200} {:answer/id #uuid "d28e2617-36fa-5a83-91a7-c27fad8cc58b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702203}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702195} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e8a34b1-a7b0-5283-a35f-ab795174db12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "27f538e6-3a40-5cca-9260-34cb318a5311" :question/problem "Find $\\det(A)$ for\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Expand across the top row with signs $+,-,+$. Delete each entry's row and column to form its minor, then subtract the diagonal products. Terms with a zero top-row entry vanish.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M_{13}&=\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(-3)\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot (-3) \\\\ &=15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(A)&=0M_{11}-0M_{12}+4M_{13} \\\\ &=0-0+4(15) \\\\ &=0+0+60 \\\\ &=60.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702189 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1394d136-f8f9-57a3-9f0a-c3e286173ef1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702173} {:answer/id #uuid "174b62fc-dbeb-50e4-ab6d-b7a14e5ad4a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702174} {:answer/id #uuid "2054a175-5501-5925-bdbd-b27df2dd2d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702177} {:answer/id #uuid "8d03c1ea-9f68-5cf7-9b61-cac5a90c95fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702194} {:answer/id #uuid "f2af173c-dbaa-58a3-b304-8d080b6c325a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702205}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702205} :answer-field/id #uuid "d19b8bf5-d930-5bdc-8fed-208bfb89e51c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702202}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7b1018af-8db7-54d9-8f9d-5f9e448245dc" :question/problem "Find $\\det(B)$ for\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Expand across the top row with signs $+,-,+$. Delete each entry's row and column to form its minor, then subtract the diagonal products. Terms with a zero top-row entry vanish.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M_{11}&=\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(-1)\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot 3 \\\\ &=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(B)&=(-2)M_{11}-0M_{12}+0M_{13} \\\\ &=(-2)(-3)-0+0 \\\\ &=6+0+0 \\\\ &=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702193 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "061668bf-68da-55d1-905d-e4840a75c7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702172} {:answer/id #uuid "51675161-0457-520a-949d-8f6c42d28fae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702182} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb1d1a9-a9b4-5e76-ad9e-7348c9dcb1ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702183} {:answer/id #uuid "63255542-9081-5a04-9979-5abf86c3eb1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702184} {:answer/id #uuid "b40d3797-e5a3-561f-b50c-213463d9e126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702198}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702198} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b4d66c1-4b31-5a17-9020-6a4cb8176c6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702176}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "894a1779-5abe-556b-b7ca-6c1329ba3e3d" :question/problem "Find $\\det(A)$ for\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Expand across the top row with signs $+,-,+$. Delete each entry's row and column to form its minor, then subtract the diagonal products. Terms with a zero top-row entry vanish.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M_{12}&=\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(-2)\\cdot (-2)-(-2)\\cdot (-3) \\\\ &=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(A)&=0M_{11}-4M_{12}+0M_{13} \\\\ &=0-4(-2)+0 \\\\ &=0+8+0 \\\\ &=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702201 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a0a77b3-270c-51dc-86b0-d79e93d6bc97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702175} {:answer/id #uuid "3be9b142-95fd-5f1a-a739-ded781f3a963" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-47" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702180} {:answer/id #uuid "639c6576-ff94-5583-98ff-6cff49ea78f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "51" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702185} {:answer/id #uuid "705575a6-e862-573b-b062-a2ab7c921e61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702186} {:answer/id #uuid "bcb185c3-1174-5c7e-9d23-2789e6f3a81c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702199}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702175} :answer-field/id #uuid "af61b8dc-f0de-5b25-8dc6-cae854777e96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702197}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cbe01429-0923-517b-9811-4f1361396dd6" :question/problem "Find $\\det(B)$ for\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Expand across the top row with signs $+,-,+$. Delete each entry's row and column to form its minor, then subtract the diagonal products. Terms with a zero top-row entry vanish.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M_{13}&=\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(-1)\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot 4 \\\\ &=-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(B)&=0M_{11}-0M_{12}+3M_{13} \\\\ &=0-0+3(-15) \\\\ &=0+0-45 \\\\ &=-45.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702206 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "271985fc-849d-5c6f-84f9-fb17bdea924e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702178} {:answer/id #uuid "73fdf215-0af2-5906-8f1f-a0a404f10f59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702187} {:answer/id #uuid "824853c3-7927-5bd2-b743-a1a851fc064b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702190} {:answer/id #uuid "832883f3-0155-54ee-a93e-a5852ae41de3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702191} {:answer/id #uuid "df373f17-d4ae-5fab-8303-249654b71451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702204}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702191} :answer-field/id #uuid "83bcbfaf-5792-5b2c-bdd7-63cad00fcc68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fbca6234-160e-5051-b9a2-11ba344fff02" :question/problem "Find $\\det(C)$ for\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Expand across the top row with signs $+,-,+$. Delete each entry's row and column to form its minor, then subtract the diagonal products. Terms with a zero top-row entry vanish.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M_{12}&=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=2\\cdot 1-(-4)\\cdot (-2) \\\\ &=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(C)&=0M_{11}-3M_{12}+0M_{13} \\\\ &=0-3(-6)+0 \\\\ &=0+18+0 \\\\ &=18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702214 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0227bc7e-d685-5eb6-939f-5a01c324b026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702208} {:answer/id #uuid "062003e6-95bf-52bb-baef-87af08c37cbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{17}{46}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702210} {:answer/id #uuid "3e1de013-5fd5-5143-bf5a-d428a8910393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{46}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702213} {:answer/id #uuid "5674f606-9746-582e-8787-06fae88e667f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702218} {:answer/id #uuid "fb6e89e5-bf1e-53cb-b02d-5eb55a84aeab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{46}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702241}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702213} :answer-field/id #uuid "191fd38b-2d03-5167-adae-cae0a939b28a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702212}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4286bde8-6293-54c6-a779-7a01b005727a" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{bmatrix}1 - 2 p & 5 & 2 p + 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ \nis $-38,$  find the value of $p.$" :question/worked-solution "Expand along the first row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Compute the three signed contributions separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{1} & =(1 - 2 p)\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1 - 2 p)((3)(2)-(0)(-2)) \\\\  & =(1 - 2 p)(6) \\\\  & =6 - 12 p\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{2} & =-(5)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(5)((1)(2)-(0)(5)) \\\\  & =-(5)(2) \\\\  & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{3} & =(2 p + 1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2 p + 1)((1)(-2)-(3)(5)) \\\\  & =(2 p + 1)(-17) \\\\  & =- 34 p - 17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the signed contributions to obtain the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =T_1+T_2+T_3 \\\\  & =- 46 p - 21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet the determinant equal to the given value.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- 46 p - 21 & =-38 \\\\ - 46 p & =-17 \\\\ p & =\\frac{17}{46}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $p=\\frac{17}{46}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702228 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f912c0e-d287-5eac-9cc6-bf5595ee0621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{64}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702225} {:answer/id #uuid "a2642eb2-2c52-5d3f-bdfc-d67b3e491a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{62}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702226} {:answer/id #uuid "dbc1d1a6-a72f-5b04-b706-26c401d4a6a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{64}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702235} {:answer/id #uuid "dca7faab-be12-5ec6-8c1e-c5aa8bf517b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{64}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702236} {:answer/id #uuid "edec8f1e-ed05-570a-bf71-a6069f3eb632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{7}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702237}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702225} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c087f21-8e66-5a8a-a89c-7842e1a09466" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702217}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bd2949b5-dacf-54db-85a1-9dea06bbf3d8" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2 k + 1 & 3 & k \\\\ -5 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is singular." :question/worked-solution "Expand along the first row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Compute the three signed contributions separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{1} & =(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}3 & k \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)((3)(1)-(k)(0)) \\\\  & =(-1)(3) \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{2} & =-(1)\\begin{vmatrix}2 k + 1 & k \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(1)((2 k + 1)(1)-(k)(-5)) \\\\  & =-(1)(7 k + 1) \\\\  & =- 7 k - 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{3} & =(-4)\\begin{vmatrix}2 k + 1 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-4)((2 k + 1)(0)-(3)(-5)) \\\\  & =(-4)(15) \\\\  & =-60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the signed contributions to obtain the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =T_1+T_2+T_3 \\\\  & =- 7 k - 64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA singular matrix has determinant $0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- 7 k - 64 & =0 \\\\ - 7 k & =64 \\\\ k & =- \\frac{64}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $k=- \\frac{64}{7}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702231 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fb8d5f1-e706-5323-8c8f-14ff06591a57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702211} {:answer/id #uuid "6a727532-45a1-5be4-aea1-dcb6e07446d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{33}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702219} {:answer/id #uuid "cc266b5f-2b9b-5e4f-9a19-04e629103fa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702230} {:answer/id #uuid "d4ae454c-7621-568b-89e6-816ea80f6e66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{37}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702233} {:answer/id #uuid "fc555972-cd60-5717-aacc-23a96420df87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{47}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702242}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702233} :answer-field/id #uuid "b00de1cb-feca-5d11-886d-c45b2091bc4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702227}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d0a66ca1-e7f8-58ff-87f8-fbd4e590ca05" :question/problem "Given that \n$$\n\\displaystyle C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & q & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ \nand $det(C)=-20,$ find the value of $q.$" :question/worked-solution "Expand along the first row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Compute the three signed contributions separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{1} & =(2)\\begin{vmatrix}q & 5 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2)((q)(1)-(5)(-2)) \\\\  & =(2)(q + 10) \\\\  & =2 q + 20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{2} & =-(-5)\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(-5)((-1)(1)-(5)(0)) \\\\  & =-(-5)(-1) \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{3} & =(1)\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & q \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)((-1)(-2)-(q)(0)) \\\\  & =(1)(2) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the signed contributions to obtain the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =T_1+T_2+T_3 \\\\  & =2 q + 17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet the determinant equal to the given value.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 q + 17 & =-20 \\\\ 2 q & =-37 \\\\ q & =- \\frac{37}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $q=- \\frac{37}{2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702234 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03c52eb1-dc93-5f62-b593-84edcb93caf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{23}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702209} {:answer/id #uuid "95ee1035-3b87-56e4-ab21-928fcc409ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702223} {:answer/id #uuid "96bf0a1b-1970-5070-acd0-dd618a6b6bf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702224} {:answer/id #uuid "c69cbe1a-4074-5045-9635-8e7c332178b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702229} {:answer/id #uuid "f900eb6b-5591-55dd-9655-25858be26923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702240}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702229} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dd4e691-7e81-5f27-bdff-2f4705d6d80d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702222}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d6547f0c-f724-5854-949b-655cae6b55c2" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 2 k + 1 & 3 & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is singular." :question/worked-solution "Expand along the first row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Compute the three signed contributions separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{1} & =(-3)\\begin{vmatrix}3 & k \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-3)((3)(1)-(k)(0)) \\\\  & =(-3)(3) \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{2} & =-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}2 k + 1 & k \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(-2)((2 k + 1)(1)-(k)(1)) \\\\  & =-(-2)(k + 1) \\\\  & =2 k + 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{3} & =(-4)\\begin{vmatrix}2 k + 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-4)((2 k + 1)(0)-(3)(1)) \\\\  & =(-4)(-3) \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the signed contributions to obtain the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =T_1+T_2+T_3 \\\\  & =2 k + 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA singular matrix has determinant $0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 k + 5 & =0 \\\\ 2 k & =-5 \\\\ k & =- \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $k=- \\frac{5}{2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "468b982b-642a-5d50-a1df-99188a41f00d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702215} {:answer/id #uuid "4927d35d-4bc6-5d7f-9f04-43cfcb4b8ab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{45}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702216} {:answer/id #uuid "842d4bbc-062c-512a-88ad-b8b1603e5b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{45}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702220} {:answer/id #uuid "84a14750-ec19-5110-ad4a-520f0a6e72bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702221} {:answer/id #uuid "ee38bff1-f26b-55dd-8bf9-1c3b2a7a0e0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{45}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702238}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702220} :answer-field/id #uuid "d15386a3-0a85-595c-8df3-84e439cd8766" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702232}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f4b3cff5-a90f-51c6-a399-b775816b7817" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $x$ given that the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ x & -1 & - x\\end{bmatrix}$ is singular." :question/worked-solution "Expand along the first row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Compute the three signed contributions separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{1} & =(3)\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & - x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(3)((-3)(- x)-(2)(-1)) \\\\  & =(3)(3 x + 2) \\\\  & =9 x + 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{2} & =-(4)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ x & - x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(4)((1)(- x)-(2)(x)) \\\\  & =-(4)(- 3 x) \\\\  & =12 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{3} & =(8)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ x & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(8)((1)(-1)-(-3)(x)) \\\\  & =(8)(3 x - 1) \\\\  & =24 x - 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the signed contributions to obtain the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =T_1+T_2+T_3 \\\\  & =45 x - 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA singular matrix has determinant $0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}45 x - 2 & =0 \\\\ 45 x & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{45}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{2}{45}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702251 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a31b24b-f166-5326-960c-1bfe96ce3869" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x\\,\\mathbf i+3y^2\\,\\mathbf j-2z\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702244} {:answer/id #uuid "305f7b77-aea1-5cf1-bcea-4e1bc308e347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\,\\mathbf i+y^2\\,\\mathbf j-z\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702245} {:answer/id #uuid "5d53c2f6-95d5-5ac9-b20e-4ff57a5d1061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x\\,\\mathbf i+3y\\,\\mathbf j-2z\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702248} {:answer/id #uuid "b2b2f464-b213-54a7-874a-11f8ca819842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x\\,\\mathbf i+3y^2\\,\\mathbf j+2z\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702260} {:answer/id #uuid "fffb41df-88f0-5fed-98b1-a8b317cb7a0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3y^2\\,\\mathbf i+2x\\,\\mathbf j-2z\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702264}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702244} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f957760-90aa-5333-b135-85d12e0aeb97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702253}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "745544fb-f75a-5f70-bc27-853dc5a97a2e" :question/problem "Find $\\nabla g(x,y,z)$ given that $g(x,y,z)=x^2+y^3-z^2.$" :question/worked-solution "Treat the other two variables as constants in each partial derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g_x(x,y,z)&=2x+0-0=2x \\\\ g_y(x,y,z)&=0+3y^2-0=3y^2 \\\\ g_z(x,y,z)&=0+0-2z=-2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlace the partial derivatives in the $x,y,z$ order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla g(x,y,z)&=g_x\\,\\mathbf i+g_y\\,\\mathbf j+g_z\\,\\mathbf k \\\\ &=2x\\,\\mathbf i+3y^2\\,\\mathbf j-2z\\,\\mathbf k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702257 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c635baa-dcec-5657-a2ae-1371ff588c4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{xy(z+1)}\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\mathbf i+\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\mathbf j+\\frac{1}{z+1}\\,\\mathbf k\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702247} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2e27f9-8bc6-5b2b-b1e1-8bd6e1686705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{xy(z+1)}}{2}\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\mathbf i+\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\mathbf j+\\frac{1}{z+1}\\,\\mathbf k\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702249} {:answer/id #uuid "7a3e1094-d0e0-5e14-ba9c-ba5c8407bb83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{xy(z+1)}}{2}\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\mathbf i+\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\mathbf j+\\frac{1}{z}\\,\\mathbf k\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702252} {:answer/id #uuid "cf494932-46e0-5a90-8f4d-23b13709e6f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{xy(z+1)}}\\left(\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j+\\mathbf k\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702262} {:answer/id #uuid "e1d19fe5-4bba-5718-a1cb-08b49e1aff53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{xy(z+1)}}{2}\\left(x\\,\\mathbf i+y\\,\\mathbf j+(z+1)\\,\\mathbf k\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702263}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702249} :answer-field/id #uuid "b66fef42-9a9c-54be-ac2a-b8a57914524c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9683deb8-0b92-537b-9b6c-5353d20f25a6" :question/problem "Given $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{xy(z+1)}$ for $x>0$, $y>0$, and $z>-1$, find $\\nabla f(x,y,z).$" :question/worked-solution "Apply the chain rule while holding the other two variables constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_x(x,y,z)&=\\frac{y(z+1)}{2\\sqrt{xy(z+1)}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{xy(z+1)}}{2x} \\\\ f_y(x,y,z)&=\\frac{x(z+1)}{2\\sqrt{xy(z+1)}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{xy(z+1)}}{2y} \\\\ f_z(x,y,z)&=\\frac{xy}{2\\sqrt{xy(z+1)}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{xy(z+1)}}{2(z+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe stated domain makes all denominators nonzero. Assemble the gradient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla f(x,y,z)&=f_x\\,\\mathbf i+f_y\\,\\mathbf j+f_z\\,\\mathbf k \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{xy(z+1)}}{2}\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\mathbf i+\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\mathbf j+\\frac{1}{z+1}\\,\\mathbf k\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702259 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41044ddf-2a72-59ef-8b6e-21709f0a3446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{e^2\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\left(\\mathbf i+\\left(2-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\,\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702246} {:answer/id #uuid "8087ffd1-93af-52fb-8908-96eb7402102f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{e^2\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\left(\\mathbf i+2\\,\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702254} {:answer/id #uuid "83abcbad-aa3f-5a59-b18a-bdc67abe04c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{e^2\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\left(\\mathbf i+\\left(2+\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\,\\mathbf j+\\mathbf k\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702255} {:answer/id #uuid "85c38537-5185-52d2-ab07-3d88982837d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{e^2\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\left(2\\,\\mathbf i+\\left(1-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\,\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702256} {:answer/id #uuid "aed08e14-a34e-5de5-8dce-6e1aab12b825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{e^2\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\left(\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702258}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702246} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fcc0e46-f953-56fd-a25d-5d22756bcd8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "af1be92d-6c3b-5df7-b03e-eb365537222e" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\nabla h(x,y,z)$ at $(2,1,\\frac{\\pi}{4})$ if $h(x,y,z)=e^{xy}\\cos(yz).$" :question/worked-solution "In the $y$ partial derivative, both factors depend on $y$, so use the product rule as well as the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h_x(x,y,z)&=ye^{xy}\\cos(yz) \\\\ h_y(x,y,z)&=xe^{xy}\\cos(yz)-ze^{xy}\\sin(yz) \\\\ h_z(x,y,z)&=-ye^{xy}\\sin(yz).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssemble the gradient in coordinate order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla h(x,y,z)&=h_x\\,\\mathbf i+h_y\\,\\mathbf j+h_z\\,\\mathbf k \\\\\n&=ye^{xy}\\cos(yz)\\,\\mathbf i \\\\\n&\\quad+e^{xy}(x\\cos(yz)-z\\sin(yz))\\,\\mathbf j \\\\\n&\\quad-ye^{xy}\\sin(yz)\\,\\mathbf k.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the stated point, $xy=2$, $yz=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$, and $\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h_x(2,1,\\tfrac{\\pi}{4})&=\\frac{e^2\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\\nh_y(2,1,\\tfrac{\\pi}{4})&=e^2\\left(2\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\\nh_z(2,1,\\tfrac{\\pi}{4})&=-\\frac{e^2\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla h(2,1,\\tfrac{\\pi}{4})& \\\\\n&=\\frac{e^2\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\left(\\mathbf i+\\left(2-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\,\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
